{
  "description": "Every Reactor contribution point the SDKs define: one id, one contract, in both SDKs unless typescript is null (a point only Python hosts use, its note saying why). test_reactor_points.py and reactor-points.test.mjs hold each SDK to this file, and docs/docs/concepts/contribution-points.mdx lists it. members are the contract's methods and attributes in Python's spelling; TypeScript spells them in camelCase, except where typescript_members says otherwise. default is the contribution id of the SDK's own default (order 100), null when the host must contribute one. tenant names what a tenant-scoped contract receives, null when the point is not tenant-scoped.",
  "points": [
    {
      "id": "pap.discoveryTransport",
      "role": "personal-agent",
      "python": "DISCOVERY_TRANSPORTS",
      "typescript": "DiscoveryTransports",
      "contract": "DiscoveryTransport",
      "members": ["get"],
      "typescript_members": ["fetch"],
      "default": {"python": "httpx", "typescript": "fetch"},
      "resolution": "single",
      "tenant": null,
      "note": "Each language's HTTP idiom: Python's transport gets one approved URL within its MetadataFetch bounds (connecting only to the approved addresses); TypeScript's is a fetch, the URL safety policy approving each URL first."
    },
